response_content:
Jill’s annual salary is  

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{Teaching} &: 20\text{ $/hr} \times 35\text{ hrs/week} \times 50\text{ weeks} = \$35{,}000 \\
\text{Coaching} &: 30\text{ $/hr} \times 15\text{ hrs/week} \times 50\text{ weeks} = \$22{,}500 \\
\hline
\text{Total} &: \$35{,}000 + \$22{,}500 = \boxed{\$57{,}500}
\end{aligned}
\]

The bird’s net southward displacement is  

\[
\begin{aligned}
&10\text{ h}\times 30\ \text{mph}=300\text{ mi (south)}\\
&2\text{ h}\times 18\ \text{mph}=36\text{ mi (north)}\\
&5\text{ h}\times 22\ \text{mph}=110\text{ mi (south)}
\end{aligned}
\]

Net distance south = \(300 - 36 + 110 = 374\) miles.

So the distance between the bird’s northern home and her southern home is **374 miles**.

The average shoe size is  

\[
\frac{5\text{ (Sophie)} + 5 \times 5\text{ (Charlie)}}{2}
= \frac{5 + 25}{2}
= \frac{30}{2}
= 15.
\]

**Answer: 15**.
